  "title": "6 Ways to Reduce Stress In College",
  "slug": {
    "_type": "slug",
    "current": "6-ways-to-reduce-stress-in-college"
  },
  "publishedAt": "2025-03-28T10:58:54",
  "excerpt": "College life is not always about having fun with friends. There will be lots of stress about completing your assignments [&hellip;]",
  "content": [
    {
      "_key": "5fe78f3ab06c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b82ce49ab619",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " College life is not always about having fun with friends. There will be lots of stress about completing your assignments and projects, and examinations as well as making time for yourself. However, having stress is normal and you should not worry about having one much. There are lots of ways to help you reduce stress. Here we have collected the 6 best ways to reduce stress."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0f5a8b206edc",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "be85f4be252f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Get Enough Sleep"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c82c8df59408",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "27c2207b8c99",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It is often said by our parents to study all the time instead of sleeping. But it is wrong. Sleep is really important for you to stay healthy. When it comes to stress, sleep is even more important. Therefore, take enough rest to decrease your stress level. Insufficient sleep can even put you at risk for serious illnesses, such as diabetes, obesity, and depression. An adult needs seven to nine hours of sleep. Thus, align your sleep schedule and get enough rest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "4e7167f872db",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "4fb5e99c979a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Eat Well"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "5af38dff91ae",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1b91060e7309",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You may not feel it but a healthy diet really helps you to decrease your stress. Make sure to eat a diet that is rich in vegetables, fruits, and whole grains. When you are stressed, you will feel like eating junk foods. Afterward, you will feel tired and you look for the same junk food to kick you back up. This will be an endless cycle making you feel worse. Therefore, start eating healthy and avoid junk foods."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "cd6abfe143ba",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "5170d4c8b44e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Exercise"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "2928c3fd325d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1e29720223e4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When you exercise, your body releases endorphins. It is a feel-good chemical that acts as a natural painkiller and even improves sleep. Therefore, get up and do some exercise. Give yourself 20 minutes a day of physical activity and it will help to reduce your stress level. You can go swimming or do some yoga. If they are not your cup of tea, try walking or jogging."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "d5ca2c76ec01",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9add429e38b7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Make a Plan"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "1ecec9839d78",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1b7b669571eb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One of the reasons you can get stressed is when you don’t have a proper schedule and there is too much work to do. Instead of worrying in these times, just get organized and make a plan. You can buy a diary, write down your to-do list, prioritize your work and stick to it. This will not only lessen your burden but helps you give enough time to your friends and families as well."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
